# Repro: bus_005 dangling-segment audit (bigHalf, bundle 67).
#
# Same setup as bigHalf.buda, but generates candidates for ONLY bus_005 via
# `generate_topologies_for_bundle bus_005` (src/dst auto-derived from the
# netlist) instead of the whole design.  This narrows the candidate pool to
# the one bus so its dangling segments are easy to eyeball.
#
# A "dangling" segment is one of two kinds (see tools/scan_dangling.py and
# set_drop_dangling):
#   A. a TRULY-dangling stub  — a ConnSeg with a single, non-block connection
#      (a wire whose other end connects to nothing); DetailedNUTS silently
#      shrinks it, which is why NUTS-level viz never flagged it.
#   B. an UNBOUNDED slide window — the +/-2^30 no-clamp sentinel on an
#      OOB-detour trunk (set_drop_dangling clamp bounds these).
#
# Finding on this fixture (2026-07-23): every Category-A stub is a TRUNK_*+MST
# hybrid (the MST-relay artifact), confirming the hypothesis for genuine
# dangling stubs.  Category-B unbounded windows are a SEPARATE class that also
# appears in pure OOB trunks (TRUNK_V_OOB / TRUNK_H_OOB), not only MST.
# Run `python3 tools/scan_dangling.py flow/big_data_test/bigHalf_bus005_dangling.buda bus_005`
# for the categorized per-candidate table.
source ../tracks/tracks4top.buda
source tc3a_flat_5x.buda
run_bundler
generate_topologies_for_bundle bus_005
# All candidates, with per-segment connectivity, so dangling stubs are visible:
dump_topologies bus_005 --conn
# Audit every candidate (not just the selected one) for connectivity opens:
check_design topo all
